{"question": "How do I sell to customers?", "slug": "how-do-i-sell-to-customers", "verdict": "Sell like a partner who already understands their business: price like the vendors they already buy, sell the outcome, and run the big deals yourself.", "notes": ["Discounting a product nobody wants makes it look worse, not better [2].", "Good sales doesn't feel like sales: they bring a problem, you solve it, and both sides walk away happy [4].", "Before you pitch, answer this: if you were your customer's CEO, what would your top three problems be? [5]", "Price the way the vendors they already pay price. Weird pricing (seashells) breaks the buyer's brain [6].", "With AI skeptics, sell the outcome, not the AI, and use AI speed: a working prototype by the second meeting [7][8].", "In enterprise, the CEO originates the big deals and fixes them when they go wrong. Hiring a salesperson and looking away is the opposite [9]."], "created": "2026-10-23T23:49:15", "clips": [{"video": "fd-FozFpTH4", "start": 187.0, "end": 188.5, "beat": "Cold open", "kind": "intro", "note": "", "card": "beat", "title": "Real vs Fake Startups", "year": "2025", "source": "Dalton + Michael", "speaker": "", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fd-FozFpTH4&t=187s", "words": []}, {"video": "yfx_0y7-qDA", "start": 0.0, "end": 14.26, "beat": "The burrito", "kind": "intro", "note": "", "card": "none", "title": "How Great Founders Approach Sales", "year": "2026", "source": "Dalton + Michael", "speaker": "", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yfx_0y7-qDA&t=0s", "words": []}, {"video": "yfx_0y7-qDA", "start": 18.25, "end": 27.54, "beat": "Startup sales screw-ups", "kind": "intro", "note": "", "card": "none", "title": "How Great Founders Approach Sales", "year": "2026", "source": "Dalton + Michael", "speaker": "", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yfx_0y7-qDA&t=18s", "words": []}, {"video": "yfx_0y7-qDA", "start": 90.81, "end": 138.58, "beat": "Good sales doesn't feel like sales", "kind": "clip", "no